# 🛰️ Scenario Evaluator v1  
## Sextant Orbital Resilience Framework

---

## 🧭 Overview

The Scenario Evaluator is a core analytical module of the Sextant Orbital Resilience Framework.

It converts deterministic simulation outputs into measurable resilience intelligence.

It operates strictly as an evaluation layer and does not perform simulation or control logic.

---

## 📍 File Location

core/evaluation/scenario_evaluator_v1.py

---

## 🧠 System Role

The evaluator sits between simulation and metrics output.

It is responsible for interpreting system states and producing structured resilience scores.

### Responsibilities:
- Interpret scenario outputs
- Analyze node states
- Compute resilience metrics
- Produce standardized evaluation reports

### Non-responsibilities:
- No simulation execution
- No control or actuation logic
- No real-world system interaction
- No scenario modification

---

## ⚙️ Core Function

Transforms system state snapshots into resilience indicators:

- System Stability Index (SSI)
- Cumulative Failure Index (CDI)
- Fragmentation Index (FI)
- Degradation Rate (DR)
- Composite Resilience Score (CRS)

---

## 📥 Input Structure

A scenario input is a deterministic state object:

```json
{
  "nodes": [
    "satellite_A",
    "satellite_B"
  ],
  "expected_states": {
    "satellite_A": "HEALTHY",
    "satellite_B": "DEGRADED"
  }
}

{
  "SSI": 0.75,
  "CDI": 1,
  "FI": 0.5,
  "DR": 0.3,
  "CRS": 0.12
}
